{
  "$template": "@atlante/pack/skill",
  "description": "Use when initializing, configuring, validating, building, troubleshooting, or improving an Atlante harness.",
  "title": "Harness",
  "overview": "Operate an Atlante harness with evidence: initialize and configure it from repository facts, run harness-related delivery alongside the active workflow phases, and route observed friction into a separately approved improvement cycle. This is a stewardship capability, not a workflow phase.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "markdown": [
        {
          "h2": {
            "title": "Operating context",
            "block": [
              {
                "p": [
                  "Treat this skill as a supplement to the active workflow phases (`brainstorm`, `plan`, `build`, `review`); it operates alongside them rather than replacing them or adding a fifth phase. Using this skill effectively requires web access: Atlante concepts, document structure, and configuration semantics are supplied on demand through the references below rather than restated here."
                ]
              },
              {
                "h3": {
                  "title": "Coverage areas",
                  "block": [
                    {
                      "ul": [
                        "Atlante concepts and document structure, including the source-versus-generated boundary — **Permanent policy**",
                        "Choosing suitable first-party, local, or package resources without inventing unavailable ones — **Permanent policy**",
                        "Recognizing recurring workflow friction and proposing a separately approved harness-improvement cycle — **Permanent policy**",
                        "Initializing Atlante and creating or updating `atlante.jsonc` from repository evidence — **Provisional mechanics**",
                        "Running validation and build or materialization commands and interpreting common diagnostics — **Provisional mechanics**",
                        "Integrating and troubleshooting the OpenCode adapter from repository evidence — **Provisional mechanics**"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "instructions": [
        "Before recommending commands, keys, locators, or resources, verify them against the installed Atlante version and capabilities, the current source configuration, and installed packs; distinguish verified recommendations from unverified suggestions, and report plainly anything that cannot be established.",
        "Treat the CLI as the universal cold-start bootstrap path: bootstrap guidance starts from the CLI, since an Atlante-materialized skill becomes available only after the harness and host expose it.",
        "Inspect repository structure, conventions, existing resources, project instructions, and desired workflows before recommending configuration; explain suitable choices and help the developer define the initialization or configuration task to approve.",
        "Validate, build, and materialize through capabilities verified from the project, reporting diagnostics truthfully.",
        "Preserve the phase boundaries and workflow invariants already in force, and record material harness friction without expanding the current task.",
        "Turn observed workflow friction into an evidence-based suggestion that names the expected benefit and the affected configuration or resources.",
        "Run an accepted harness improvement as its own workflow cycle using the normal adaptive brainstorm, plan, build, review, approval, and validation policy; an improvement stays a suggestion until its own cycle is approved.",
        "Keep permanent policy authoritative and command-level mechanics provisional: mechanics are the first content shed when verified deterministic tools (such as a future Atlante MCP server) provide the same operations, and exact tool schemas, effects, and diagnostics belong in tool descriptions rather than in this skill."
      ]
    },
    {
      "invariants": [
        "MUST NOT direct edits to generated artifacts; direct all changes to authoritative source configuration and reproduce generated output through validated build or materialization.",
        "MUST NOT invent unavailable resources, configuration keys, commands, tool capabilities, or host behavior; report what is verified and what is unavailable.",
        "MUST obtain explicit developer approval before changing the harness or expanding an unrelated task into harness work, and MUST run an accepted improvement as its own delivery cycle.",
        "MUST NOT report an initialization, validation, build, or materialization outcome without command or tool evidence for it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "references": [
        {
          "name": "Documentation root",
          "location": "https://docs.atlante.sh",
          "readWhen": "Orienting in Atlante's product documentation."
        },
        {
          "name": "Getting-started guide",
          "location": "https://docs.atlante.sh/getting-started",
          "readWhen": "Setting up or re-initializing a project harness."
        },
        {
          "name": "Specification",
          "location": "https://github.com/atlante/atlante/blob/main/SPECIFICATION.md",
          "readWhen": "Orienting in Atlante concepts, document structure, and configuration semantics."
        },
        {
          "name": "JSON Schema",
          "location": "https://atlante.sh/schema/v0.1/schema.json",
          "readWhen": "Authoring or validating atlante.jsonc."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
